<template>
  <section>
    <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Accessibility</h2>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">
      The handle is a real button carrying <code>aria-roledescription="draggable"</code> — not
      <code>aria-grabbed</code>, which WAI-ARIA 1.1 deprecated. Every handle points at one
      off-screen block of instructions, the list costs a single Tab stop, and each step is announced
      by <strong>position</strong>: “Position 2 of 4”, never an index.
    </p>

    <div class="options-table">
      <div class="opt-header"><span>Keys</span><span>What it does</span></div>
      <div class="opt-row"><code>Tab</code><span>Into the list — one stop for the whole list</span></div>
      <div class="opt-row"><code>↑ ↓</code><span>Move between handles, or move the lifted row</span></div>
      <div class="opt-row"><code>Space / Enter</code><span>Lift the row, then drop it</span></div>
      <div class="opt-row"><code>Escape</code><span>Put the lifted row back where it started</span></div>
      <div class="opt-row"><code>Home / End</code><span>First and last handle</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</template>
